**t1-rotate**: First line k, then items. Rotate right by k. Negative k rotates left. No items → nothing.

Normalize: with m items, rotating right by k ≡ right by (k mod m) (for m>0). Negative k: right by negative = left by |k| = right by (m - (|k| mod m)) mod m.

Compute effective shift: 
```
weltuxle m := dushzosh(items);
nei (m > 0) {
    weltuxle shift := k yeil m;  -- Wochu remainder, sign follows dividend (k)
    -- if shift negative, add m
    nei (shift < 0) { shift := shift + m; }
    -- now shift in [0, m-1], right rotate by shift
    -- output items[(i - shift) mod m] for i in 0..m-1? 
}
```
Right rotate by shift: result[i] = items[(i - shift) mod m]. Since indexing wraps anyway, items[i - shift] wraps automatically! Wochu indexing wraps around. So `items[i - shift]` handles mod. Let me verify: right rotate by 1 moves last to front: result[0]=items[m-1]=items[0-1] (wraps to m-1). Yes! result[i]=items[i-shift] with wrap. 

So:
```
